IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p2`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch6`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch6.l4 (Schedule 6). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 6`

§§ `Paragraph 1(a), (b) -- the disabilities taken into account`

-- Argument order: subject to it as a result of the loss of faculty; may be expected to be subject during the period; involves loss of
-- earning power or expense; also results from another cause; regulations under 1(b) provide it is taken into account.
-- A disability from the loss of faculty, expected to continue: taken into account, whether or not it involves loss of earning power or expense.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not expected to continue during the period, or not a result of the loss of faculty: not taken into account (the text's no).
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a result of the loss of faculty, even with another cause: 1(b) is about disabilities "resulting from the relevant loss of faculty", so FALSE.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Also from another cause: only regulations decide; silent regulations give NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraphs 1(c), 1(d) and 2 -- circumstances; 100 per cent; handedness`

#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's age` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's sex` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's physical condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's mental condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other particular circumstance: the text says no.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 1(c) any other particular circumstance of the claimant` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Handedness: paragraph 2 only says nothing in 1(c) PREVENTS regulations making different provision, so the Act itself answers NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` `sch 6 para 2 the claimant's being right-handed or left-handed` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 1(d): a prescribed loss of faculty is 100 per cent whatever the assessor judges; otherwise the assessor's figure; none given -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` TRUE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` FALSE (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- adjusting earlier assessments: none is reduced`

-- Argument order: the existing assessment; the percentage the regulations' adjustment gives.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 3 the assessment after the adjustment` 40 30 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 3 the assessment after the adjustment` 40 50 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 3 the assessment after the adjustment` 40 40 EQUALS 40

§§ `Paragraph 6(1) -- the period begins no earlier than the end of the 90 days`

-- An accident on Monday 4 November 2024: the 90 days end Saturday 15 Feb 2025, so the earliest first day is Sunday 16 Feb 2025 (see the Sch 7 Part II tests).
-- A period of suffering that began 1 January 2025 is cut back to start 16 February 2025; its last day is untouched.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(1) the period taken into account by the assessment` (Date 4 11 2024) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 16 2 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026
-- A period of suffering that began 1 March 2025, after the 90 days, starts then.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(1) the period taken into account by the assessment` (Date 4 11 2024) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026
-- Starting exactly on the first day after the 90 days: unchanged.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(1) the period taken into account by the assessment` (Date 4 11 2024) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 16 2 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 16 2 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2026

§§ `Paragraph 6(2) -- provisional assessments`

#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(2) a provisional assessment is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(2) a provisional assessment is made` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 6(2)(b): "shall begin with the end of the period" read as the day after (NOTES.md): a provisional period ending 30 June 2025 -> 1 July 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(2)(b) the day the period taken into account by the next assessment begins` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
-- Across a year end and a leap day: ending 28 Feb 2024 -> 29 Feb 2024; ending 31 Dec 2025 -> 1 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(2)(b) the day the period taken into account by the next assessment begins` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2024, `the last day` IS Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(2)(b) the day the period taken into account by the next assessment begins` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 1 1 2026

§§ `Paragraph 6(3) to (5) -- the 14 per cent rule`

-- Argument order: the assessed extent; assessed at different percentages for different parts; the latest part's percentage; the (4)(a) aggregation seems
-- likely; the (4)(b) aggregate seems likely to reach 14 per cent or more.
-- Under 14, a single percentage, no aggregation: final.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 13.99 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 14 or more: (3) does not speak; NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 14 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 30 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): both limbs (aggregation AND aggregate of 14 or more) must hold for (3) to be disapplied.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5)(a): different percentages for different parts: (3) does not apply unless the latest part is under 14.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 10 TRUE 14 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 30 TRUE 13.99 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 30 TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5) is "subject to (4)": the aggregation exception still disapplies (3).
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` 5 TRUE 10 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 6(3): the final assessment's period cannot end before the earliest date the extent seems likely to be under 1 per cent.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the period taken into account may end on the day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the period taken into account may end on the day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 6(3) the period taken into account may end on the day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 2 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- what an assessment states`

#ASSERT `sch 6 para 7 what the assessment must state` TRUE EQUALS LIST "the degree of disablement in the form of a percentage", "the period taken into account by the assessment", "whether the assessment is provisional or final"
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 7 what the assessment must state` FALSE EQUALS LIST "the degree of disablement in the form of a percentage", "the period taken into account by the assessment"
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 7 the percentage and the period may be specified more particularly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 7 the percentage and the period may be specified more particularly` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 8(2) -- the listed payments`

#ASSERT `sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` `sch 6 para 8(2)(a) a payment by way of disablement pension` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` `sch 6 para 8(2)(b) a payment by way of benefit under paragraph 4 or 7(1) of Schedule 8` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) needs a prescribing instrument: absent it, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` `sch 6 para 8(2)(c) a payment of other prescribed benefit in connection with hostilities or service as a member of Her Majesty’s forces or of another specified organisation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` `sch 6 para 8(2)(c) a payment of other prescribed benefit in connection with hostilities or service as a member of Her Majesty’s forces or of another specified organisation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Any other payment: the list is not closed by "only", so NOTHING (not FALSE).
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` `sch 6 para 8(2) any other payment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
